{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JnwVmHUWb6jyPZD4QN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made three calls you may want to change:\n\n- **The March error is in.** I put it alongside the fix, so it reads as evidence that you think like a supervisor. If he doesn't know about it, this will be the first he hears of it. That's usually better coming from you than from someone else, but it's your call. If you cut that bullet, the letter still works.\n- **The $9,000 is out.** It's the role's set pay, so naming it adds nothing and makes the letter about money. Leave it for the meeting.\n- **No claim that the role is open or that no one supervises the team.** You don't know either one, so the letter only argues that you already do much of the job.\n\nIt's about 330 words. Fill in the brackets, and send it before December 15. It's also worth asking one or two of your lawyers whether they'd back you before the January review.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Request for promotion to senior paralegal\n\nDear [Name],\n\nI'd like to be considered for promotion to senior paralegal in the January review cycle. I'd also welcome the chance to meet with you in person to discuss it before then.\n\nI've been a paralegal in the litigation group for five years. Last year I supported four lawyers on 23 cases, two of which went to trial. I billed 1,640 hours, against the group's target of 1,550.\n\nA senior paralegal supervises the other paralegals, and I already do much of that work:\n\n- **Training.** I trained all three paralegals the group has hired in the past two years.\n- **Systems.** In 2023 I built the tracking sheet the group uses for court deadlines. Two other groups in the firm have since adopted it.\n- **Managing risk.** Last March I entered a filing deadline incorrectly in that sheet. Another paralegal caught it, and we filed two hours before the court's cutoff. I then added a second-person check to the sheet, so every deadline is now confirmed by someone other than the person who entered it. Every group that uses the sheet has that check.\n\nAs senior paralegal, I would make this work official: setting standards for the team, bringing new hires up to speed, and keeping our deadline process reliable as the group takes on more work.\n\nCould we find 30 minutes in the next few weeks? I'm happy to work around your schedule.\n\nThank you for considering this.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":783,"cache_read_input_tokens":9903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":783},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"276e98bb-37dc-4309-ab97-500b97e30723","uuid":"db6351fb-ff68-4c38-929e-e1dfb63adbb1","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:21:31.439Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7JnwLqHKSiks7cHqm5h"}
